course: dictionary
lesson: 5451
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Landlord is one of them. «Damp is when walls get wet inside and grow black mould; in a rented home the landlord is supposed to fix it.» Here a landlord is the person or company that owns a house, flat or room and rents it out.
explain: The clues are rented, rent and fix. Families pay rent to the landlord, so the landlord owns the home. Now try the other meaning: «In a UK story, the landlord served drinks behind the bar.» Serving drinks and the bar are the clues, so here a landlord is the man who runs a pub.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits these clue words? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A landlord is a person or company that owns a house, flat or room and rents it to people for money.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, a landlord can also be the man who runs a pub.
fact: Families who rent pay rent to the landlord every week or month.
fact: «A landlord is allowed to raise the rent, usually with warning, and a rise leaves less money for other things.»
fact: Phrases to know: the landlord, pay the landlord, pub landlord.
exercise: «In a rented home the landlord is supposed to fix the damp.» Who is supposed to fix the damp? | The family who rents the home | The bank | The school | *The landlord
exercise: «A landlord is allowed to raise the rent, usually with warning.» What does a rise in rent leave families with? | Free food | A bigger garden | *Less money for other things | More money for other things
exercise: In a UK story, «the landlord served drinks». What is the landlord in this story? | A bus driver | A teacher at a school | A farmer who grows apples | *The man who runs a pub
test: A family pays 500 pounds rent to the landlord each month. How much do they pay in 3 months? | 2000 | 1000 | 1200 | *1500
test: «Some families rent their home from a landlord.» In this sentence, who owns the home? | *The landlord | The family | The bank | The school
exam: Mira says a landlord is always a man who serves drinks. Is she right? | *No, a landlord can own a flat that a family rents, and in the UK a landlord can also run a pub | No, a landlord only works on farms | Yes, because landlord means a friend | Yes, a landlord always works in a pub
